   684	// ---- fix-1 (codex §9 round 2 [P1]) — the THREAT MODEL, measured ------------
   685	//
   686	// Transcript:
   687	// `dev/plans/runs/codex/0.8.20/slice-22-review-round2-targeted-20260729T004445Z.log`.
   688	//
   689	// The finding is correct as stated: a writer who can compute the current digest
   690	// forces the probe to be skipped. These four tests establish what that is worth —
   691	// that the SAME actor already defeated the SAME arm before the cache existed, and
   692	// that a known digest expires at the next change to any fingerprint input.
   693	//
   694	// fix-2: same actor, NOT same cost — the marker route is the cheaper one, and that
   695	// concession is §8.4 of the design note. The bound on the finding is the ruled
   696	// residual above, not these tests.
   697	
   698	/// **THE HYPOTHESIS TEST.** Is the pre-slice design tamper-evident against a hostile
   699	/// writer? No — and this is the measurement that says so.
   700	///
   701	/// **fix-2 — read the scope of this measurement carefully.** It establishes that the
   702	/// same actor had a route that defeats the probe while it runs in full. It does NOT
   703	/// establish that the two routes cost the same: this one needs the drifted backend's
   704	/// 45 exact embeddings, the marker route needs a publicly computable digest. fix-1
   705	/// drew "the cache adds no new attack surface" from this test; that inference was
   706	/// wrong and is struck (§8.4).
   707	///
   708	/// The 0.8.18 probe re-embeds the 45 committed probes and compares them to the
   709	/// STORED references. Those references live in an ordinary table in the same file.
   710	/// An actor with write access re-baselines them to their drifted backend's own
   711	/// output — same ordinals, same texts, same identity triple, same blob lengths, so
   712	/// the fix-2 completeness validation sees nothing — and the probe then verifies the
   713	/// drifted backend against itself and PASSES.
   714	///
   715	/// The cache is removed from the picture entirely: the marker is DELETED before
   716	/// the open, and the test asserts all 45 embeds actually happen. What runs is the
   717	/// check body as shipped at the slice baseline `fe85337f` (the TC-68 diff over that
   718	/// function adds only the cache gate and the `record_probe_verification` call).
   719	///
   720	/// The control leg proves the forgery is what does it: the identical drifted
   721	/// backend against an UN-forged baseline is caught and refuses dense.
   722	#[test]
   723	fn a_forged_stored_baseline_defeats_the_probe_even_when_it_fully_runs() {
   724	    // -- control: drift alone, with the cache out of the way, IS caught. --------
   725	    let control_dir = TempDir::new().unwrap();
   726	    let control_path = db_path(&control_dir);
   727	    let control_calls = counter();
