   329	### 8.1 The finding, accepted
   330	
   331	> `probe_verification_is_cached` trusts any `_fathomdb_open_state.value` exactly
   332	> equal to the freshly computed SHA-256. That is fail-safe for absent, corrupt,
   333	> truncated, non-TEXT or stale values because they miss and run the probe. It is
   334	> not fail-safe for an attacker-modified row: the fingerprint inputs are
   335	> deterministic, public DB and build inputs, not a secret or an engine-authenticated
   336	> marker, so a writer can forge the current digest and force the early
   337	> `return Ok(())` before the 45-probe verification runs.
